{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1674 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "21ac0cae70b6399681bda65691032e364ad2b1f7434fe423cd70141893d5ca8e" :edb/db-before-t 1673 :edb/db-after-t 1674 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534986 50 #inst "2026-10-08T13:23:13.066Z" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161704 1100 "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x}$, where $\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ Evaluate the function when $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161704 1100 "The linear form $f(\\mathbf{x})$ is defined as $f(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{a} \\mathbf{x},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e104f037293e19fe2a12d9b2e14cc344d5cca06f933f393755cf03568b5702c0.png)  Evaluate the function when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/8832f5ec6073de4098b3b0f856a3ab5e000926a9d09f76e87909adb67777cc17.png)" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161704 1145 "Substituting ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4c5ce198c2271b51807f4c17fffdf4288c524ff73469196bd481dc489c5a0e40.png) we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 8+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-15+0+20 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161704 1145 "Substituting $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= ax \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-5) + 0 \\cdot 8 + 4 \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-15 + 0 + 20 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161705 1100 "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$, given by\n\n$B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1$\n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161705 1100 "Consider the the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})= 2 x_1y_2 - x_2y_2 +3 x_2y_3-x_3y_1\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y})$ when ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/dcea1a36972408a1f6a56577f61150bd8e4c2b91284820ca47c632a985d912ca.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/f9885ea740945a64e44931aca4befbd4022a84ae0fa1454627f2b44133eb4651.png)" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161705 1145 "We are given that\n\n$\\qquad$ $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2} \\\\ y_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(x, y) &= 2x_{1}y_{2} - x_{2}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{3} - x_{3}y_{1} \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot 2 + 3 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 - (-1) \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&= 4 - 2 + 3 - 2 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161705 1145 "We are given that \n\n$\\qquad$ ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/652258046237288de7102e402a266dd3afff1abfecf97aa2156a351a7611afb3.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/58ef5fbadaf595035dc902aac9b66bbce61fea79b6a4144ed060f0486dda982c.png) \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{3}-{x}_{3}{y}_{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =4-2+3-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161706 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4dfdcd2e2f0d80ee8b6633b0dd4bc33b477b22e4db0f2ad36cbfa62eef702659.png)\nConsider the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/15fa693fff5bc0eb2a8851089612b5a3fb969c3fd5fbc7c0821e58e52ff4260d.png) above.  Write down a bilinear form ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/7c7f59284956b7a02d9d9d16387cfba529479fb49aa8efff3bfa908be0fbb04f.png) in terms of the components of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/ed54028979894fad0ac2b928c90c9eeea9361d1c8514fb61ee8ce28435ac2a5c.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/9849708035aaa18397dfafbbcdfeb923f576296406c494c30093477f6b2aaa33.png)" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161706 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Write down a bilinear form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{y}$ in terms of the components of $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161706 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e8f54943816e5af3ad7a3b92ff68887d8126962ffcba1d3109d10390616d8a04.png) of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/3397629141c3034fbd4b5cd5bd8c554676175a4b1e3f5eccd26cc5d66ee1bec8.png) corresponds to the term ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/e4b6d1207e1c34e37c760af85eb4a4e5594e3db2da2c4ba4841a4106de188c1b.png) in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/734889027df1469d75a4506f295a277b908081224b5860ebf9ec8ea432053dd9.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/4ccd64cd17dd595c826e5a8bf13d4bf991c57d128d7a3fbca5a49eaf265f0867.png)" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161706 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{T}Ay &= 2x_{1}y_{1} + (-1)x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} + (-2)x_{2}y_{2} \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} - 2x_{2}y_{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{T}Ay &= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} & x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}y_{1} \\\\ y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} & x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2y_{1} - y_{2} \\\\ 3y_{1} - 2y_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= x_{1}(2y_{1} - y_{2}) + x_{2}(3y_{1} - 2y_{2}) \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} - x_{1}y_{2} + 3x_{2}y_{1} - 2x_{2}y_{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161707 1100 "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161707 1100 "The matrix of the bilinear form $B(\\mathbf{x},\\mathbf{y}) = 2x_1y_1 + 2x_2y_1 - x_3 y_2+2x_3y_3$ is given below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & c & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161707 1145 "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB(x, y) &= 2x_{1}y_{1} + 2x_{2}y_{1} - x_{3}y_{2} + 2x_{3}y_{3} \\\\\n&= 2x_{1}y_{1} + 0x_{1}y_{2} + 0x_{1}y_{3} \\\\\n&= + 2x_{2}y_{1} + 0x_{2}y_{2} + 0x_{2}y_{3} \\\\\n&= + 0x_{3}y_{1} + (-1)x_{3}y_{2} + 2x_{3}y_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$, $b=2$, and $c=-1$. Finally,\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3\n$$" 13194139534986 false] [17592186161707 1145 "Each term $a_{ij}x_i y_j$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry $a_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}-{x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,2{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{y}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{3}{y}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043646/assets/24b1e29dccdff51c2ca2c7780a8a5dfcf9c74ed91d48afdde8a14c5127f89ce1.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-1.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+2+(-1) = 3.\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186161912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324943 13194139534986 true] [17592186161912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324950 13194139534986 true] [17592186161912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324971 13194139534986 true] [17592186161912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324985 13194139534986 true] [17592186161912 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324992 13194139534986 true] [17592186161913 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324957 13194139534986 true] [17592186161913 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324978 13194139534986 true] [17592186161913 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324999 13194139534986 true] [17592186161913 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325006 13194139534986 true] [17592186161913 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325013 13194139534986 true] [17592186161914 1020 #edb/ref 17592186324964 13194139534986 true] [17592186161914 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325020 13194139534986 true] [17592186161914 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325027 13194139534986 true] [17592186161914 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325034 13194139534986 true] [17592186161914 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325041 13194139534986 true] [17592186161915 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325048 13194139534986 true] [17592186161915 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325055 13194139534986 true] [17592186161915 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325062 13194139534986 true] [17592186161915 1020 #edb/ref 17592186325069 13194139534986 true] [17592186162541 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534986 true] [17592186162541 1100 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186162541 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}a & -2 \\\\ 0 & b\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nThe matrix of the bilinear form $B(x, y) = x_{1}y_{1} - 2x_{1}y_{2} + 2x_{2}y_{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a + b$?" 13194139534986 false] [17592186162541 1145 "Each term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form corresponds to the entry ${a}_{ij}$ of the matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{y}_{1}\\,+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, the corresponding matrix of the bilinear form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+2=3.\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324943 1017 #edb/ref 17592186324944 13194139534986 true] [17592186324943 1089 "q-140851" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324943 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534986 true] [17592186324943 1100 "The linear form $f(x)$ is defined as $f(x)=ax,$ where $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$  Evaluate the function when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324943 1113 #uuid "6f7eba9d-d05c-525c-ab4e-f81697290353" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324943 1145 "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6-5+4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324945 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324946 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324947 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324948 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1000 #edb/ref 17592186324949 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1041 "selection" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1104 #edb/ref 17592186324945 13194139534986 true] [17592186324944 1110 #uuid "5b204740-ab27-57d6-9100-2e78a25c8998" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324945 1034 "-7" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186324945 1111 #uuid "d774ccb2-55a3-51c4-b063-5c1ce6c59b89" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324946 1034 "-5" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324946 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186324946 1111 #uuid "b55c4d70-fcb9-51d5-8580-67966effce3d" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324947 1034 "3" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186324947 1111 #uuid "78284014-2038-500e-8bde-0d780e7975b8" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324948 1034 "-3" 13194139534986 true] [17592186324948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186324948 1111 #uuid "8d133599-1d18-53f9-81f1-5843a1cbcbb2" 13194139534986 true] [175921863249