13194139534986 true] [17592186325012 1111 #uuid "811e68ab-4958-5d37-a487-b99a7cd5352e" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325014 13194139534986 true] [17592186325013 1089 "q-93981" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534986 true] [17592186325013 1100 "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)=2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325013 1113 #uuid "89f0af3e-6ee2-57cd-b64e-9c8bc1644265" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325013 1145 "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{2}-4{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{3}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0-4\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0-24-1-0 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325015 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325016 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325017 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325018 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325019 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1041 "selection" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325019 13194139534986 true] [17592186325014 1110 #uuid "44b6b4d3-b63a-57b0-80ce-016894df75d2" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325015 1034 "-26" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186325015 1111 #uuid "e535bbe9-a2ef-56af-95a6-776ce09c5c49" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325016 1034 "23" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186325016 1111 #uuid "becf0d5f-85cd-5974-9d9b-ec2f7a7e3c3c" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325017 1034 "-22" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186325017 1111 #uuid "1eff6a69-a0d0-5c3b-9b87-234f92543203" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325018 1034 "27" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186325018 1111 #uuid "674014d7-02a8-5bab-95bf-062c4a27a3c4" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325019 1034 "-25" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534986 true] [17592186325019 1111 #uuid "43519f53-0b98-502a-8d69-116ad9444328" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325020 1017 #edb/ref 17592186325021 13194139534986 true] [17592186325020 1089 "q-93983" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325020 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534986 true] [17592186325020 1100 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding bilinear form ${x}^{T}\\,Ay$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325020 1113 #uuid "e4aa981a-46cc-5351-93da-92c0a2d35b7c" 13194139534986 true] [17592186325020 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{y}_{j}$ in the expression of the bilinear form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ay & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+1{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{1}{y}_{2}+{x}_{2}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a bilinear form in terms of vector components, we compute the follow